course: dictionary
lesson: 14196
title: Motorboat: a boat with an engine
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are built from two smaller words. Motorboat is made of motor and boat. A motor is an engine, and a boat carries people across water. Put them together and you get a boat that moves with an engine.
explain: The word gives you a clue. A motorboat does not need sails or oars. «The family took the motorboat across the lake, and Dad did not need to row once.» Rowing is what you do with oars, so the sentence tells you the motorboat moved by itself, with its engine.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «The family took a sailboat across the lake.» That is a different kind of boat. Only the motorboat fits the clue: it runs on an engine, not on wind or muscle power.
fact: A motorboat is a boat that moves with an engine, not with sails or oars.
fact: «The motorboat zipped across the lake.» Zipped means moved very quickly.
fact: Safety rule: always wear a life jacket on a motorboat, and keep your hands and feet away from the propeller, the spinning blades under the water.
fact: Speed is distance divided by time. If a motorboat travels 30 kilometres in 1 hour, its speed is 30 kilometres per hour.
fact: On a river, a motorboat goes faster downstream, with the current, and slower upstream, against the current.
exercise: «The motorboat has an engine, so it does not need oars.» What moves a motorboat? | The wind | Oars | *An engine | Sails
exercise: Which word means a boat that moves with an engine? | *Motorboat | Canoe | Rowboat | Sailboat
exercise: Mia says a motorboat moves with sails. What is the right meaning? | A boat that always sinks | A boat with oars only | *A boat that moves with an engine | A boat with sails
test: «Dad steered the motorboat slowly upstream, against the river current.» Why was the motorboat slower? | Its sails were up | It had no engine | It was going downstream | *It was moving against the current
test: Which safety rule is correct on a motorboat? | *Wear a life jacket | Sit on the engine | Dangle your hands in the water | Stand on the seats while it moves
exam: «The motorboat raced across the lake, covering 40 kilometres in one hour.» What was its speed? | 4 kilometres per hour | 400 kilometres per hour | *40 kilometres per hour | 1 hour per kilometre
